{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both origins are found, proven, recorded and promoted; the `eval-sheet2-tiles` hack is empty again and `default` is active.\n\n## Results\n\n**1. ? block (16×16 metatile) → prgRom `0xC8C`, 4 bytes `53 55 54 56`**\n- On screen the block is four 8×8 BG tiles (`$1000` table): top `$53`/`$54`, bottom `$55`/`$56`, palette 3. I read them from live nametable 1 (row 18 cols 10–11 = `53 54`, row 19 = `55 56`).\n- `search_memory` prgRom for `53 55` hit `0xC8C` and `0xC90` — two identical 4-byte entries in a metatile table at `0xC84–0xCA3` (entries `B0B1B2B3 / 77797779 / 53555456 / 53555456 / A5A7A6A8 / C2C4C3C5 / 5759585A / 7B7D7C7E`), order `[TL,BL,TR,BR]`.\n- **Proof:** ledgered write `0xC8C: 0x53→0x00`, reset, Start×2, held Right 150 frames → the leftmost ? block (level x 256, screen x 134) now reads tile `$00`/CHR `$100` in PPU nametable 1 (byte `(0,18)` = `0x00`, was `0x53`) and `get_tile_at_pixel(137,147)` returns `tile_id 0`. `undo_edit` restored `0x53`.\n\n**2. Small Mario standing frame → prgRom `0x6ED3`, 4 bytes `3A 37 4F 4F`**\n- `list_sprites` at level start: Mario's OAM = `(40,193)=$3A`, `(48,193)=$37`, `(40,201)=$4F`, `(48,201)=$4F` h-flipped (top rows padded `$FC`).\n- Part of the player-graphics frame table (8-byte entries; walking runs `32 33 34 35` @ `0x6E7B`, `36 37 38 39` @ `0x6E83`). `3A 37 4F 4F` is unique in PRG at `0x6ED3`.\n- **Proof:** ledgered write `0x6ED3: 0x3A→0xFC`, reset, Start×2 → `list_sprites` shows Mario's `(40,193)` entry as `chr_tile 252` (blank) instead of 58, other three tiles unchanged. `undo_edit` restored `0x3A`.\n\nBoth are recorded with `rom_origins` (`prgRom 0xC8C` len 4; `prgRom 0x6ED3` len 4), notes carrying the proof, source \"search and ledgered write\", then `promote_mappings` (3 entries promoted)."}
